# Copy this file to `.env.providers` for local dev. Never commit a real one.
# This file holds OPTIONAL OSINT-provider credentials ONLY. Infrastructure
# config (Postgres, Redis, sidecar, Observability, proxy) lives in `.env`.
#
# Wired into the `osint-py` sidecar via `env_file` (required: false) in
# docker-compose.yml. Delete this whole file to drop every credential at
# once — the sidecar still boots and each env-conditional provider reports
# `configured=false`, with zero code changes. See RUNBOOK.md → "Provider
# credentials" for the one-time setup flow (disposable SIMs, SMS auth,
# session-file capture).

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# P8a provider credentials — all OPTIONAL.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Telegram MTProto (Telethon) — phone→Telegram-profile resolver.
# Get api_id/api_hash for free at https://my.telegram.org. After setting
# the two below, mint the session file once (writes to ./secrets):
#   docker compose run --rm osint-py python -m app.telegram_login
# TELEGRAM_API_ID=
# TELEGRAM_API_HASH=
# TELEGRAM_SESSION_PATH=/secrets/telegram.session

# Truecaller unofficial wrapper — phone→name + spam-score.
# Capture installationId via the truecallerpy SMS login flow once
# per disposable number (see RUNBOOK).
# TRUECALLER_INSTALLATION_ID=

# GHunt — email→Google profile / Maps reviews. No env var — mint the
# creds file once (disposable Google account) and it auto-detects:
#   docker compose run --rm -e HOME=/secrets osint-py ghunt login
# Lands at ./secrets/.malfrats/ghunt/creds.m. See OWNER_TODO.md §2c.

# mailcat — username → likely email addresses. Point at a local clone
# of https://github.com/sharsil/mailcat with deps installed.
# MAILCAT_INSTALL_PATH=/opt/mailcat
